    text:"Cleveland Clinic, RIKEN and IBM Team were named finalists for the 2026 ACM Gordon Bell Prize for quantum-centric supercomputing: uniting IBM Quantum Heron processors with Fugaku, Miyabi-G and ROQUO classical supercomputers to simulate a biologically meaningful protein containing 12,635 atoms, the largest molecular system yet modeled using quantum computers. The team achieved a 40× scale increase and 210× accuracy improvement in less than a year; their method models how potential medicines interact with protein targets while reducing computational demands and manual errors.",
